# Internationalization

AttentionX uses **two i18n stacks**. Pick the one that matches the surface you are editing.

## Popup / onboarding / prompt / shared React UI

- Strings live in `public/locales/*.json` (flat dot-keys, e.g. `wizard.title`, `common.save`)
- Runtime loads these via `@lib/i18n.js` (`initI18n()` at entry points, then `t('key')` or `t('key', { count })`)
- Supported languages: `en`, `es`, `pt`, `de`, `fr`, `it` (see `SUPPORTED_LANGUAGES` in `src/lib/i18n.ts`)
- Interpolation uses `{param}` braces (not `{{param}}`)
- Add the same key to **every** locale file under `public/locales/` when introducing copy
- Prefer `t()` for new user-facing strings; do not mass-migrate existing hardcoded English unless you are already editing that component

## Content script (X Shadow DOM UI)

- Strings live in `src/i18n/resources.ts` (nested keys under `translation.content`, etc.)
- Use the bundled `i18next` instance: `i18n.t('content.card.trust')` with `i18nOptions` from `resources.ts`
- Supported languages: `en`, `da` only
- Interpolation uses i18next `{{param}}` syntax
- Keep `resources.en` and `resources.da` structurally identical; `src/i18n/resources.test.ts` enforces this
- Keep the content script as a self-contained IIFE via `vite.content.config.ts`

## Legacy / avoid for new work

- `src/App.tsx` uses `react-i18next` + `resources.ts` — legacy dev shell, not the live popup
- `src/i18n/react.ts` wires react-i18next but is not the primary popup path
- Root `locales/*.json` duplicates `public/locales/`; **`public/locales/` is the runtime source** — update it (and mirror root copies only if you are syncing both deliberately)

## General rules

- Do not localize protocol values, event kinds/tags, URLs, storage keys, relay addresses, or log identifiers
- Use interpolation for counts and runtime values instead of string concatenation
- Cockpit pages and some panels (e.g. `AttentionXPanel`) still have hardcoded English — treat as migration debt; localize incrementally when touching that code
- Add or update `src/i18n/resources.test.ts` when changing content-script locale structure; add locale parity checks when adding popup languages
